{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KZLEgVQFzUvYLU1TiFZRjY","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Exclude territories (PR, VI) and aggregate farmers markets\ntotal_fm = fm.filter(~fm.state_abbr.isin(['PR', 'VI'])).aggregate(total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Get US population from census\nus_pop = census.filter(census.NAME == 'United States').select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    total_fm.join(us_pop, xo.literal(1) == xo.literal(1))\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=total_fm.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I can see that the data includes the 50 states, District of Columbia, and territories like Puerto Rico (PR) and Virgin Islands (VI). According to the user's request, I need to exclude territories. The 50 states + DC would be the main U.S. entities to include.\n\nActually, let me reconsider - the user said \"total farmers markets (excl. territories)\". Looking at the data, I see:\n- 50 states (CA, NY, PA, etc.)\n- District of Columbia (DC)\n- Puerto Rico (PR) - this is a territory\n- Virgin Islands (VI) - this is a territory\n\nSo I need to sum all farmers_markets except PR and VI. Let me check if there are any other territories.\n\nActually, thinking about this more - when the user says \"total farmers markets (excl. territories)\", they probably want the count for the mainland U.S. (the 50 states + DC). Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands are definitely territories.\n\nLet me create a metric that:\n1. Sums farmers markets from all states except territories (PR and VI)\n2. Gets the U.S. population from the census data\n3. Calculates the rate per 100,000\n\nI should create a build script that does this calculation to keep both sources in the lineage.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a script to calculate the metric across both datasets:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KZLEgVQFzUvYLU1TiFZRjY","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Exclude territories (PR, VI) and aggregate farmers markets\ntotal_fm = fm.filter(~fm.state_abbr.isin(['PR', 'VI'])).aggregate(total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Get US population from census\nus_pop = census.filter(census.NAME == 'United States').select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    total_fm.join(us_pop, xo.literal(1) == xo.literal(1))\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=total_fm.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":838,"cacheRead":20889,"cacheWrite":638,"totalTokens":22378,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.00419,"cacheRead":0.0020889000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.0007975,"total":0.007089400000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":298},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911879116,"responseId":"msg_011Ce744WGzHrNfRv5UVffVG","rawStopReason":"tool_use"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"toolu_01KZLEgVQFzUvYLU1TiFZRjY","toolName":"write","args":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so)\n\n# Exclude territories (PR, VI) and aggregate farmers markets\ntotal_fm = fm.filter(~fm.state_abbr.isin(['PR', 'VI'])).aggregate(total_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Get US population from census\nus_pop = census.filter(census.NAME == 'United States').select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    total_fm.join(us_pop, xo.literal(1) == xo.literal(1))\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=total_fm.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}
